      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PALLADIUM NZ (4) was a beaten favourite in the Victoria Derby last start but he did have to work so was far from disgraced when just over 4m from the winner. Impressive winner of his Derby heat prior and produced two strong efforts here last month including an easy win from a much wider draw. The drop to the mile is some query but he has the speed to go forward from this draw. NEPTUNITE (2) did a great job to come from much wider and score by 3 metres over this distance at his first visit to this circuit last start. Tackles some good opposition here but his strike rate is impressive and a low draw helps. WICKED CONFESSION (1) comes off a placing from a much wider barrier in the Ladyship Cup last start at Melton. Tackles the boys this time but is well served by the ace draw. A wide barrier presents a challenge to last-start winner I GOT CHILLS NZ (11) but his form is hard to knock. His stablemate HUXTON NZ (8) is also good enough to feature with some luck on his side.",
